Subject: add a /run tier to the OS configuration file search
Source: downstream patch for AppStream 1.1.1
Upstream: not submitted; needs agreement on the /run/appstream.conf path

as_context_ensure_os_config_loaded() (src/as-context.c:608-654) selects
one complete OS configuration file and loads it with
g_key_file_load_from_file(): the first file that exists wins completely,
and the function never merges keys from more than one file. Before this
patch the selection checked only two tiers in order, SYSCONFDIR
"/appstream.conf" then AS_DATADIR "/appstream.conf". meson.build:38-43
defines SYSCONFDIR from get_option('prefix') / get_option('sysconfdir'),
and Meson's sysconfdir option special-cases a /usr prefix to resolve to
/etc rather than /usr/etc, so with the package manifest's
--prefix=/usr that constant already compiles to /etc: a path the
administrator can write. AS_DATADIR resolves to
${prefix}/share/appstream, i.e. /usr/share/appstream, where this
package's own build already installs its vendor appstream.conf. Both
tiers were already correct. There was no /run tier, so a deployment could
not supply transient FreeRepos policy between the vendor default and the
administrator's file, and a boot could not override the vendor default
without writing into the persistent, administrator-owned /etc tree.

This patch adds exactly one more g_file_test() check between the
existing two, in the same "first file that exists wins" shape the
function already had: SYSCONFDIR, then the new AS_RUNCONFDIR
"/appstream.conf" (AS_RUNCONFDIR defaults to "/run"), then AS_DATADIR.
The selection stays whole-file: whichever tier's file is chosen still
supplies every key the reader will see, exactly as before this patch,
because as_context_ensure_os_config_loaded() treats the chosen file as
the complete configuration for the running process rather than a
fragment to combine with the other tiers. A missing file in any tier
stays silent, as it already did for the pre-existing two tiers:
g_file_test() with G_FILE_TEST_EXISTS returns FALSE without touching the
filesystem's error state, and the function only calls g_debug(), never
g_warning(), when it cannot open the file it selected. The existing
g_debug ("Loading OS configuration from: %s", as_config_fname) call is
unchanged and still names whichever file the three-way selection above
it actually chose.

Neither this patch nor the package installs anything under /etc,
/usr/etc, or /run: /run/appstream.conf is only a compiled-in search path
that this package does not populate.
--- a/src/as-context.c
+++ b/src/as-context.c
@@ -607,0 +608,4 @@
+#ifndef AS_RUNCONFDIR
+#define AS_RUNCONFDIR "/run"
+#endif
+
@@ -622 +626,2 @@
-	/* load data from /etc, but fall back to the default in /usr/share if the override does not exist */
+	/* load data from /etc, then /run, then fall back to the vendor default in /usr/share
+	 * if neither override exists */
@@ -623,0 +629,2 @@
+	if (!g_file_test (as_config_fname, G_FILE_TEST_EXISTS))
+		as_config_fname = AS_RUNCONFDIR "/appstream.conf";
